.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library is the client for the
.Dv system.Network
system network broker.
The broker follows the Casper model: it performs DNS and socket operations
under an immutable, session-derived policy and returns
.Em real, connected, rights-limited socket descriptors .
It never proxies application data and exposes no emulated socket handle.
The caller owns all I/O on the returned descriptor.
.Pp
The
.Fn networkcmp_client_open
function consumes the local broker session channel that
.Xr switchboard 8
injects.
The library creates one process-wide, token-correlated session, performs the
initial negotiation with
.Fn networkcmp_hello ,
and records the negotiated values; repeated opens return references to that
same authority.
.Pp
.Fn networkcmp_client_open_admin
opens the same protocol through
.Dq system.Network.Admin ,
a name that requires the
.Dq system.network.admin
software attribute.
Only approved programs declaring that attribute, such as
.Xr networkcmpctl 8 ,
resolve it, including from a login session that cannot resolve
.Dq system.Network .
A process uses one interface for its lifetime; opening the other one fails
with
.Er EBUSY .
.Pp
The reply returned by
.Fn networkcmp_client_limits
is the binding contract for the features, and the resolve
result bound.
There is no global lookup or fallback path.
.Pp
.Fn networkcmp_connect
policy-checks the destination
.Fa address ,
opens and connects a TCP socket to it, and stores the connected descriptor in
.Fa out_fd .
.Fn networkcmp_udp
opens a datagram socket, connects it to
.Fa peer ,
and returns that descriptor; a connected UDP socket exchanges datagrams only
with its peer.
Both accept an
.Vt AF_INET
or
.Vt AF_INET6
.Vt sockaddr .
The returned descriptor is delivered out of band over the session channel with
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
and is limited before delivery to only the rights a data path needs:
.Dv CAP_READ ,
.Dv CAP_WRITE ,
.Dv CAP_EVENT ,
.Dv CAP_SHUTDOWN ,
.Dv CAP_GETSOCKOPT ,
.Dv CAP_SETSOCKOPT ,
.Dv CAP_FCNTL
.Pq Dv F_GETFL and Dv F_SETFL for Dv O_NONBLOCK ,
.Dv CAP_FSTAT ,
and
.Dv CAP_IOCTL
restricted to
.Dv FIONREAD , FIONBIO ,
and
.Dv FIOASYNC .
It cannot bind, connect, listen, accept, or be transferred again.
A denied or failed request returns
.Li -1 ,
sets
.Va errno
to the broker's connect status, and leaves
.Fa out_fd
set to
.Li -1 .
.Pp
.Fn networkcmp_connect_ex
is
.Fn networkcmp_connect
with a client-supplied handshake deadline
.Fa timeout_ms
in milliseconds: the broker connects non-blocking and, if the TCP handshake does
not complete within the deadline, fails the request with
.Er ETIMEDOUT
and delivers no descriptor.
A
.Fa timeout_ms
of zero is identical to
.Fn networkcmp_connect
.Pq a fully blocking connect with the kernel default timeout .
.Pp
.Fn networkcmp_resolve
implements bounded
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 Ns -style
forward resolution without exposing provider or resolver descriptors.
The caller supplies the result-array capacity through
.Fa nresults ;
on success it contains the number returned.
An optional canonical-name buffer and TTL output may be supplied; a TTL of
zero means no positive cache lifetime is advertised.
For DNS results, the provider reports the remaining minimum across address
records and CNAMEs, rounded down and aged across cached queries.
Numeric and local hosts results report zero.
The broker resolves independently of its request loop and permits one active
resolution per session; an overlapping resolution fails with
.Er EBUSY .
.Fn networkcmp_getaddrinfo
is the familiar convenience interface.
It translates the bounded results into a linked
.Vt struct addrinfo
list and returns an
.Dv EAI_*
status.
The resulting list must be released with
.Fn networkcmp_freeaddrinfo ,
not
.Xr freeaddrinfo 3 .
The
.Fa hints Ns 's
.Va ai_flags
may combine
.Dv AI_PASSIVE , AI_CANONNAME , AI_NUMERICHOST , AI_NUMERICSERV ,
.Dv AI_V4MAPPED ,
and
.Dv AI_ALL ;
any other flag fails with
.Dv EAI_BADFLAGS .
.Dv AI_ADDRCONFIG
returns
.Dv EAI_BADFLAGS
because configured source-address filtering is unavailable.
The raw
.Fn networkcmp_resolve
API rejects
.Dv NETWORKCMP_RESOLVE_F_ADDRCONFIG
with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.Dv AI_V4MAPPED
and
.Dv AI_ALL
are honored: an
.Vt AF_INET6
resolve may return IPv4-mapped IPv6 results, and with
.Dv AI_ALL
both native
.Dv AAAA
and mapped
.Dv A
results are returned.
.Pp
The library speaks the FIDL protocol
.Sy bsd.network.v1
.Pq Pa /usr/share/fidl/networkcmp.fidl ;
see
.Xr fidl 7 .
Opening the process client negotiates the wire version
.Pq Er EPROTONOSUPPORT No for an incompatible provider
and reads the session limits.
Calls from several threads proceed concurrently on the shared session;
transaction identifiers correlate replies, and one waiting thread at a time
reads the channel for all of them.
Each call is bounded by 30 seconds, shortened by an active
.Fn service_budget_begin
budget
.Pq Xr service_runtime 3 ;
a timeout fails that call with
.Er ETIMEDOUT
and cancels it, and the session stays usable.
A lost provider makes the client terminal with the transport error.
.Fn networkcmp_hello
returns the session limits
.Pq the Sy GetLimits No method .
The message framing in
.In networkcmp_protocol.h
and the validators in
.In networkcmp_server.h
describe the pre-FIDL wire format and are kept for compatibility; the
structures and constants the functions above use remain current.
The opaque client is process-bound.
The injected broker session is retained as process-lifetime authority;
.Fn networkcmp_client_close
releases a library borrow, and a later
.Fn networkcmp_client_open
reacquires the same managed session without creating another channel reader.
If the broker returns a malformed reply, the library marks this authority
terminal: the failing operation and every later operation return
.Er EPROTO
without sending another request.
After
.Xr fork 2 ,
the child cannot reuse the parent's session
.Pq Er EINVAL
and must open a separately injected authority if one exists.
.Pp
The broker provides DNS resolution, connected TCP and UDP sockets, and, for a
label whose
.Ql listen
policy permits it,
.Fn networkcmp_listen :
the broker binds and listens a TCP socket on an OS-assigned loopback port,
stores the concrete port in
.Fa *port_out
for the caller to advertise, and returns the narrowed listening descriptor in
.Fa *out_fd .
The caller
.Xr accept 2 Ns s
on that descriptor directly (capability-mode legal); accepted connections
inherit its rights.
A
.Fa backlog
of 0 selects
.Dv SOMAXCONN .
Listeners beyond those described above are not implemented.
.Pp
The
.Ql networkcmp
DTrace provider exposes component-open, message-send, message-receive, and
message-reject probes.
Provider daemons audit policy decisions through OpenBSM; client-library
activity is operational telemetry and is not audited.
.Pp
.Fn networkcmp_pf_open
opens one short session to
.Dq system.Network.PF
.Pq the Sy NetworkPf No protocol of the same library ,
negotiates the wire version, requests the one descriptor the session
delivers, closes the session and stores the descriptor in
.Fa *out_fd .
The caller's software identity must hold the
.Dq system.network.pf.read
attribute, or
.Xr switchboard 8
does not resolve the name
.Pq Er ENOENT .
The descriptor is a
.Xr pf 4
device reporting the state table of the caller's own network stack:
the provider binds it to a jailed caller's vnet before delivery.
It carries exactly
.Dv CAP_READ ,
.Dv CAP_FSTAT
and
.Dv CAP_IOCTL ,
admits only
.Dv DIOCGETSTATES
.Pq Vt "struct pfioc_states" No of Vt "struct pfsync_state" , In net/pfvar.h ,
allows no
.Xr fcntl 2
rights and cannot be transferred again; the library checks those limits on
receipt and fails with
.Er EPROTO
when the descriptor differs, and locks it against further transfer and
inheritance.
The call is independent of the process client above and bounded like the
other calls.
A provider that could not open
.Pa /dev/pf
or bind the caller's vnet reports its errno and delivers nothing.
.Sh CONCURRENT RESOLUTION
The provider can coalesce at most 16 identical concurrent requests within
one session.
Each call still receives its own reply.
Different concurrent requests and excess duplicates return
.Er EBUSY ;
a duplicate shares the original job deadline.
.Sh DNS FAILURES
When no usable address is available, an unsuccessful DNS query returns
.Er EAGAIN
through the broker protocol, or
.Er EAI_AGAIN
from
.Fn networkcmp_getaddrinfo .
Complete negative answers return
.Er ENOENT
or
.Er EAI_NONAME ,
respectively.
If one queried family fails and another returns only a negative answer,
the result remains retryable.
A usable address from either family, including IPv4-mapped IPv6 fallback,
can still satisfy the lookup.
Numeric addresses do not require a working nameserver.
.Pp
.Dv AI_V4MAPPED
with
.Dv AF_INET6
also maps numeric IPv4 literals and matching local hosts entries.
A numeric literal with
.Dv AI_NUMERICHOST
never requires DNS.
Native IPv6 hosts entries take precedence unless
.Dv AI_ALL
requests both native and mapped entries.
A matching hosts entry satisfies the lookup before DNS is attempted.
